    source: "Agent: entity_investigator (Claude API)"
    summary: "Commonwealth Fusion Systems shows the strongest technical credibility with peer-reviewed HTS magnet breakthroughs, $2B+ from sophisticated investors, MIT collaboration, and a validated tokamak approach targeting 2025-2027 for SPARC plasma experiments. Their early 2030s commercial timeline is aggressive but grounded in proven physics. TAE and Helion pursue alternative FRC approaches with less independent validation, minimal peer-reviewed publications on their core breakthroughs, and more speculative timelines. TAE's aneutronic fuel cycle faces extreme temperature barriers never demonstrated. Helion's pulsed approach and 2028 commercial claims lack scientific precedent. For Q>10 continuous operation by 2031, CFS has the most credible pathway, though even this faces significant engineering challenges beyond plasma physics."
    relevance: 0.78p
    date: 2026-03-06
}

